# Authorized remediation: One-bar Dukascopy execution defects (2026-10-12)

Execute and FIX, not just plan. User approved remediation of execution blockers. ChatGPT is final verifier. Repo /home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research. Native installed ml4t.backtest mandatory; no custom backtest loop. No live orders, no commit/push, no protected August 2026 or later.

Preflight: inspect HEAD, branch, remote, dirty status, tmux/Codex sessions. Read AGENTS.md and nested AGENTS, docs/research_sessions.md, prior scripts/run_one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011.py, tests/test_one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011.py, docs/audit/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011.md, latest Phase567 artifacts/ledgers and validation_status.json. Preserve ALL unrelated dirty files. Prior phase567 ended CODE=0; do not repeat/overwrite it. Read FULL applicable repo ML4T skill instructions (run-backtest, lookahead-bias, calendar-ops, polars-patterns, validate-data, cost-model, continuous-futures). Inspect installed ML4T Broker, Engine, ExecutionPolicy and StopFillMode implementations and public APIs before deciding how to fix them. Delegate bounded independent source or execution audit to subagents if useful.

Critical fixes:
1. Previous +$166521.58 cost-aware result used native STOP_PRICE, which grants favorable stop-trigger fills on gap opens: 3335 entry gap cases equivalent to ~$409132.58 of price advantage, and 105 protective stops did not lose additional ~$19993.80 beyond stop on gaps. This dominates net profit. Write exact synthetic stop-entry long/short gap test and stop-loss gap test. Choose native engine stop-market price semantics that fill at worse of OPEN vs trigger on gap, trigger otherwise. Inspect StopFillMode NEXT_BAR_OPEN, CLOSE_PRICE, BAR_EXTREME and fill implementations. Use native supported extension only if needed and legal under repo; no site-packages edits, no manual simulator. Don't claim an additive post-hoc dollar adjustment is a backtest.
2. 216 next-bar MARKET exits were late, likely because historical runner INNER JOIN removes all source minutes in incomplete 30-minute bins. Distinguish market EXECUTION data from valid complete 30m decision bars: retain available raw valid 1m rows for fill path, while only release completed 30m signals after their last event, and do not gate on future bar availability. Correctly exit at first minute of immediately following 30m when a source print exists, and independently record true missing opens as unresolved (no fabricated event). Test partial next bar with real open, absent next open, and DST.
3. OCO race: broker fills both opposing entry stops before strategy can cancel (one occurrence at 2024-06-07 12:30 UTC). Seek native atomic OCO/contingent order API or supported brokerage extension while keeping Engine. If both sides crossed within one 1m candle and no tick order, do not guess which filled first or choose winner after outcome; mark unresolvable and conservative sensitivity, and do not call OCO passed. Test same-minute double trigger, no hedged fake exposure, max 2 fills/day.
4. 43-44 1m entry plus protective stop within SAME candle are intrinsically ambiguous without finer timestamps. Inventory canonical tick/quote data; if unavailable record conditional bounds and unresolvable counts, NEVER hallucinate sequencing. Stop-market 1000 USD trigger is not guaranteed worst loss.
5. BID-only Dukascopy USATECH.IDX/USD is not real CME NQ. Inspect ml4t-data canonical sources and whether verified Dukascopy ASK/tick is accessible. Do not synthesize ASK as actual quote; optionally run labeled spread sensitivities. No huge download or re-writing unrelated canonical stores.
6. Independently correct/reverify diagnostics: full source-minute shift for missing opening rows (older shift after boundary filter was wrong); distinguish fill-price slippage from commission in trade gross/net, never double charge. Check all trade/account/equity reconciliation, OCO, max 2/day, rolling 50 COMPLETE PRIOR bars, exit next 30m OPEN, DST, cash/margin, gaps.
7. Keep exact original 50 bars, 30-minute session, both stop sides, next opening market exit, 1000 USD protective stop, 2/day, 1 indicative NQ contract at 20USD/point. Do not optimize, add vol filters or change account constraints to recover profitability. All already observed 2013-Jul2026 is retrospective, protected after Jul14.

Deliver new isolated files ONLY: run_log/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012/ (spec, pre-registered trial ledger, logs, outputs, source/quote audit, reconciliation, error records, hashes), scripts/run_one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.py, tests/test_one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.py, docs/audit/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.md. Preserve previous research artifacts. Begin with small synthetic causality/OCO/gap tests. Once correct, run full-history 2013-Jul14 2026 native ML4T on 1m source for zero-cost and full tick 0.25 index points adverse/fill plus 2.50 fee/fill; include realistic gap fills. If full exact behavior impossible, run bounded validated proxy stress scenario only and explicitly mark native exact-rule BLOCKED. Use persistent tmux for long simulations; record exact command, HEAD, config, log, exit, output and inspect first output. Diagnose ordinary failures, fix and rerun. After execution, run focused pytest and independendly verify ledgers/metrics/fill exceptions. No false success.

Final should report actual verified changes, corrected results if generated, and explicitly unfixable source/execution issues; status VERIFIED vs INFERENCE vs BLOCKED. No live approval.
