The broker source changes the assessment: ML4T 0.1.7’s `STOP_PRICE` path already checks the bar open and fills at that open when it has crossed the stop. The earlier “favorable stop gap” calculation appears to have used `reference_price` as the open; saved fills show `price_source=open`, so that metric is not proof of bad fills. I’ll verify long, short, and protective gaps through actual `Engine` fills and correct the reconciliation. The OCO ambiguity still blocks an exact full-history rerun.
