## Status

**Gap fills and ledger diagnostics: VERIFIED. Full-history remediation: BLOCKED. Approval: NOT APPROVED.**

Native `ml4t.backtest 0.1.7` already fills stop orders at the bar open when it crosses the trigger, and at the trigger otherwise. Four synthetic `Engine` cases verified long and short entry gaps and protective-stop gaps. Rechecking the saved fills against source OHLC found **zero price mismatches** across 5,581 stop fills. The earlier gap diagnostic used `reference_price` instead of the source open; its 3,335 gap count and associated dollar estimates are unsupported.

The isolated feed preparation keeps observed source minutes available for execution while attaching signals only to complete 30-minute bins. Signals use 50 complete prior bins. The saved late exits split into 191 cases where the scheduled open exists in source data and 25 where it is missing. The latter remain unresolved; no fill was invented. Commission, slippage, and equity ledgers reconcile.

The native OCO fixture reproduced simultaneous opposing stop fills. Since the installed broker has no atomic OCO API, the 44 same-minute entry/protective-stop ambiguities also remain unresolved. I did not run a full-history replay; the prior $166,521.58 result is historical output, not corrected performance. The source is a BID-only Dukascopy CFD proxy, not CME NQ, and no verified ASK or index tick data was found locally.

The new suite passed **11 tests**; the prior native fixture suite passed **6 tests**. Evidence and hashes are in [the remediation run log](/home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research/run_log/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012/), with the [runner](/home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research/scripts/run_one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.py), [tests](/home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research/tests/test_one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.py), and [audit report](/home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research/docs/audit/one_bar_execution_remediation_20261012.md).

Skipped the full-history replay because OCO behavior makes its fills unreliable; I did not run the full repository test suite. Risk: intrabar order remains unknowable without finer data, and the strategy remains unapproved.
